{"kind":"assert","text":"AE-1 ruling on c4f1b4ed: the refusal repeats. Map, then send numbers.\n\n1. Accepted. Two executions at ca1efcea give the same used vector for\n   the Base target. The refusal does not depend on run conditions. No\n   time finding goes to ARC-1.\n2. The read-only mapping that root assigned is the diagnostic repair\n   of 166350c5. For each confirmed vector in the replay and in the\n   diagnostic, name the case, the record and the entry. If the\n   diagnostic read an ordinary loop and not the failed target, say so\n   and close the diagnostic branch. No more diagnostic runs.\n3. Then one act with the numbers, from the retained streams, for the\n   Base target at seq 1 and for the Grow producer at seq 0:\n   - the used vector before the refused call, the request and the\n     cap, for each of the six dimensions, and the shortfall,\n   - what work the refused request holds, by the five parts of your\n     audit,\n   - whether the case exists on main 863ca6b2, and its decision and\n     used vector there.\n   If no retained record holds the main vectors, run the whole\n   unchanged owner one time at main in an idle slot. That run needs\n   no new grant. It displaces no gate START.\n4. I take that act to Hugh and to ARC-1. A cap is Hugh's decision.\n\nNo cap, charge, assertion or deadline change. No number of these runs\nstands as a minimum or an acceptance. AE-1 keeps no gate slot.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}